 In the end, the new competition proved popular with most followers and skaters, as well as the media."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The gold medals in Torino were divided by skaters from six countries, the highest number since 1968. Host nation Italy won medals for the first, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/100957"} "Enrico Fabris"] " winning two individual medals and leading the pursuit team to gold. This also made him the most successful skater, followed by " [:a {:href "/athletes/100967"} "Cindy Klassen"] ", who won five medals (including one gold), the first skater since " [:a {:href "/athletes/86551"} "Eric Heiden"] " to win 5 speed skating medals at a single Olympics."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1122"} "500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 February 2006"] "\n" [:td {} "37"] "\n" [:td {} "12"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1125"} "1,000 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "18 February 2006"] "\n" [:td {} "41"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1126"} "1,500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "21 February 2006"] "\n" [:td {} "41"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1127"} "5,000 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "11 February 2006"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1128"} "10,000 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "24 February 2006"] "\n" [:td {} "16"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/1129"} "Team Pursuit (8 laps), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "15 – 16 February 2006"] "\n" [:td {} "36"] "\n" [:td {} "8"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {}